{
  "about": "How loud a sound is heard at a time: its volume, or its volume Keyframes (in seconds from its start, each approached by its `ease`, Linear when none) sampled there, times its linear fades; silent before its `start` and after its `end` (seconds into the Clip). Its `fade_in` and `fade_out` (none when absent) are as set: when together they are longer than the sound, both are shortened by the same share to fit. A `muted` one (docs/adr/0016) is silent throughout, whatever its volume, Keyframes and fades. Each of `at` is [seconds into the Clip, the gain heard there]. Read by backend/tests/test_gain.py and frontend/src/pages/job/editor/loudness.test.ts, so that the render's gain and the preview's can't drift.",
  "tolerance": 1e-6,
  "sounds": [
